    [releases/v0.30.0][Worker][Feature] Allow probabilistic draft sampling with MRV2 PCP (#18193)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #18086 to `releases/v0.30.0`. This author-submitted PR replaces
    the bot-created backport #18153 with the same code patch.
    
    Ascend MRV2 PCP rejects `draft_sample_method="probabilistic"` during
    configuration validation, preventing it from reaching the existing draft
    sampling implementation. Remove the greedy-only check for MTP, Eagle3
    and DSpark, and update the configuration tests to accept both `greedy`
    and `probabilistic`. The speculative-method allowlist and other PCP
    configuration checks remain in place.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Ascend MRV2 PCP configuration validation now accepts probabilistic
    draft sampling for MTP, Eagle3 and DSpark. Independent restrictions,
    including fine-grained LM-head TP constraints, still apply. The sampling
    implementation is unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified that the backport patch matches merged #18086 and bot-created
    #18153. Both changed files are identical to #18153, and `git diff
    --check` passed.
    - Existing #18153 CI passed the full CPU unit tests with both the
    [verified vLLM main
    commit](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38016169613/job/114107803909)
    and [vLLM
    v0.30.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38016169613/job/114107803913).
    [Pre-commit](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38016169613/job/114106801579)
    also passed.
    - The updated `tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py` covers both
    sampling methods for all three supported speculators across the existing
    eager and graph configuration cases.
    - The previous [310P embedding
    job](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38016169613/job/114110726060)
    failed while importing the Hugging Face reference runner because PyArrow
    26.0.0 requires NumPy 2.0+, but the CI environment installed NumPy
    1.26.4. The failed embedding cases do not enable PCP or speculative
    decoding. Overall CI is not claimed passing.
    - CI for this resubmission is pending. No new NPU inference or
    distribution-correctness validation was performed for this resubmission.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
